WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:07.840
Even though 2016 was an epic year for movies,
it almost feels like a warm-up when you look

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:14.080
at the long list of blockbuster films already
on the release calendar for 2017.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.740
It's never too early to get excited about
taking a trip to the theater, so we've lined

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:26.480
up the biggest upcoming releases — and whether
you're into action, comedy, horror, or drama,

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.179
there's something here for everyone…

00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:31.749
Resident Evil: The Final Chapter

00:00:31.749 --> 00:00:38.040
Five years after Resident Evil: Retribution,
Milla Jovovich returns to close out the sci-fi

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:44.650
horror franchise she's led for more than a
decade, with nearly $1 billion in worldwide

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.650
grosses.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:50.990
Despite the long lapse between sequels, this
sixth installment will reportedly pick up

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:55.510
where Retribution left off, while following
director Paul W.S.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:01.250
Anderson's mandate to come full circle with
the saga of a dystopian future in which a

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.390
corporation-created virus has unleashed a
zombie plague.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.509
John Wick: Chapter 2

00:01:08.509 --> 00:01:14.039
After everything he went through in the first
movie, what could possibly convince John Wick

00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:15.689
to come out of retirement?

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:21.590
Dog lovers will be relieved to hear it isn't
the death of another pooch that gets his guns

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:24.569
blazing in John Wick: Chapter 2.

00:01:24.569 --> 00:01:30.130
This time, one of John's old buddies is in
the middle of a scheme to topple an assassin's

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.090
guild and he needs backup.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.759
The Lego Batman Movie

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:42.049
Not long ago, the idea of a movie "based on"
Legos seemed too silly for words, but then

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:49.529
The Lego Movie racked up nearly $470 million
while making us all root for plastic bricks

00:01:49.529 --> 00:01:53.740
— and play "Everything Is Awesome" on endless
repeat.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:55.280
"Oh my gosh I love this song!"

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.500
"Everything is awesome"

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:04.400
Taking the hint, Warner Bros. is diving right
in with a universe of Lego-derived films,

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:10.420
starting with this spin-off, which brings
back Will Arnett as Gotham's Caped Crusader.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.420
The Great Wall

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:18.550
Zhang Yimou's sprawling historical fantasy
epic The Great Wall has an intriguing — albeit

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:23.810
a little ridiculous — idea: The Great Wall
of China was built to keep out more than just

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.620
unwanted human neighbors.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:31.750
From everything we've seen so far, The Great
Wall will at least be a spectacular showcase

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.830
of effects-heavy cinematography.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.030
Logan

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:41.470
Hugh Jackman has played Wolverine for so long
that it's nearly impossible to imagine anyone

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.250
else in the role.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:49.120
Soon, 20th Century Fox will need to figure
out who'll be the next actor to play the part.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:55.440
But first, Jackman's getting his swan song
with a third standalone Wolverine feature.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:01.410
The film's plot draws from Marvel's Old Man
Logan comic books, about an alternate-future

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.120
version of the nearly ageless hero.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:09.440
The film will also feature the return of Patrick
Stewart's Professor X, adding yet another

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.400
layer of closure for longtime fans of the
franchise.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.040
Kong: Skull Island

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:21.760
On March 10, 2017, the big gorilla returns
with Kong: Skull Island.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:28.060
This '70s-set trip into the Kong mythos gives
viewers the biggest version of the character

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:33.760
they've ever seen — which is a good thing
for Kong, because after Skull Island finishes

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:40.980
its theatrical run, the studio is planning
to pit him against Godzilla in a monster mashup

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:41.980
for the ages.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:43.920
What could possibly go wrong?

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.560
(Classic Godzilla screech)

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.010
Beauty and the Beast

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:56.600
Like Disney's earlier Beauty, this version
draws inspiration from the classic fairy tale

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:02.240
about a prince, played here by Dan Stevens,
who's cursed with a grotesque appearance.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:08.340
Yet, he finds love with a pure-hearted maiden,
played by Emma Watson, who's imprisoned in

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:14.290
his castle after her father offers her up
in a deal to spare his own life.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:20.430
Like a lot of stories from the era, it's pretty
dark, but Disney's animated adaptation put

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:26.470
a family-friendly spin on it with music and
humor, and we can expect the same here — plus

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:31.900
a cast that includes Ewan McGregor and Sir
Ian McKellen.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:33.350
Power Rangers

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:38.850
The forthcoming Power Rangers isn't the first
movie to capitalize on the mighty morphin

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.050
'90s craze, of course.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:47.190
However, director Dean Israelite's take on
the story offers a much more serious and emotionally

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:54.290
charged account of how these misfit teens
managed to become a band of unlikely world

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:57.020
saviors, battling back the forces of evil.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:02.460
If the film does manage to renew even a little
bit of the Power Rangers frenzy that the series

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:07.160
enjoyed in the '90s, it's going to be massive.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.910
Ghost in the Shell

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:14.560
Rupert Sanders' adaptation of the popular
Ghost in the Shell manga series of the same

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:20.730
name is expected to be a visual spectacular
that chronicles an epic chase between a cyborg

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:23.530
policewoman and a dangerous hacker.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:29.410
It promises to offer the same kind of gnarly
effects and existential futurism that captivated

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:35.930
audiences in films like The Matrix, Scarlett
Johansson's own turn in Lucy, and The Fifth

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:37.010
Element.

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:38.180
Sign us up.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:40.400
The Fate of the Furious

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:46.030
According to the official synopsis, the new
sequel in this long-running franchise — titled

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:52.290
The Fate of the Furious — finds Vin Diesel's
Dom lured back "into the world of crime he

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:58.570
can't seem to escape and a betrayal of those
closest to him" by a "mysterious woman," played

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:01.680
by the always amazing Charlize Theron.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:07.510
Listen carefully and under the roar of the
motors, you can hear the box office cash registers

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:08.010
ringing…

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:08.990
(Cha Ching!)

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.400
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:17.660
Initially, it seemed like a hilariously dumb
idea for Marvel to turn a relatively obscure

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:23.720
comic about a ragtag team of intergalactic
do-gooders — whose ranks included a raccoon-like

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:31.360
creature and an alien resembling a sentient
tree — into a $200 million movie.

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:37.810
Nearly $775 million in box office receipts
later, Guardians of the Galaxy could be the

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:42.100
start of an Avengers-style franchise for the
studio.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:46.861
While we don't have many details regarding
what they'll be up to this time around, it's

00:06:46.861 --> 00:06:49.981
pretty much a given that it'll be tons of
fun.

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:51.360
"Nobody has any tape!"

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.420
"Not a single person has tape?!"

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:57.020
"You have an atomic bomb in your bag, if anybody's
gonna have tape it's you!"

00:06:57.260 --> 00:06:58.400
"I have to do everything!"

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.040
"You are wasting a lot of time!"

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:03.060
"I am Groooooooooot!!!!"

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:05.320
Alien: Covenant

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:10.900
Fans who feel Prometheus didn't tie into the
Alien films strongly enough might be better

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:17.840
served by Alien: Covenant, which brings back
Michael Fassbender and Noomi Rapace to show

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:23.310
what happens after they hijack an ancient
spacecraft in order to venture to the homeworld

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:28.120
of the mysterious Engineers and halt their
plans for humanity.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:31.460
Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No
Tales

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:36.090
Pre-production on the fifth installment in
the Pirates of the Caribbean saga started

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:42.650
back when the previous sequel, 2011's On Stranger
Tides, was on its way to theaters, and its

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:48.940
path through development has been strewn with
script difficulties and budget-induced delays.

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:55.860
Still, any new chapter in a franchise that's
grossed nearly $4 billion counts as a promising

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:01.990
development for the studio, and Disney has
stood by while producer Jerry Bruckheimer

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:07.680
steered Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men
Tell No Tales to its destination.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:08.990
Wonder Woman

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:15.400
After being introduced to audiences in Batman
v Superman: Dawn of Justice, Gal Gadot's Wonder

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:20.820
Woman will get her own standalone feature,
which is rumored to be the first installment

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:26.960
in a period-piece trilogy that will take audiences
from the 1920s to the present day.

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:32.579
Whatever actually happens in the movie, it's
a long-overdue victory for comics fans who've

00:08:32.579 --> 00:08:39.380
waited years for the Amazonian warrior to
get a shot at her own big-screen franchise.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.110
World War Z 2

00:08:41.110 --> 00:08:48.170
The first World War Z turned out to be surprisingly
entertaining, as well we extremely commercially

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.210
successful.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:55.620
That brings us to the inevitable sequel, World
War Z 2, in which Brad Pitt returns to battle

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:56.940
the zombie plague.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:02.930
We don't know much about the plot at this
point, but director Juan Antonio Bayona will

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:08.920
be working from a screenplay by Steven Knight,
whose varied list of credits includes the

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:13.320
chess drama Pawn Sacrifice and Bradley Cooper's
Burnt.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.420
Cars 3

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:21.760
Rev up your engines, kids, because Lightning
McQueen is back in high-speed action in Disney-Pixar's

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:22.860
Cars 3.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:30.540
The 3D animated adventure, which follows the
events of 2006's Cars and 2011's Cars 2, will

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:36.270
follow McQueen on his journey to catch up
with a new generation of speedsters and feature

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:42.230
the return of some fan favorites like Mater,
Sally Carrera, and Ramone.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:44.890
Transformers: The Last Knight

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:50.680
Aside from Mark Wahlberg being back as the
saga's current human star, The Last Knight

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:57.520
looks like it'll plunge viewers into a time-traveling
plot that includes King Arthur and an alternate

00:09:57.520 --> 00:10:04.140
history in which Nazis won World War II — plus
plenty of action and lots of lead-ins to the

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:07.620
assortment of spinoff films the studio's planning.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.490
Despicable Me 3

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:15.290
Despicable Me has grown into an impressively
adaptable franchise for Universal.

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:20.959
Details are still very sketchy regarding this
third installment, but we can safely assume

00:10:20.959 --> 00:10:27.490
Steve Carell will be back as the nefarious,
but kinda cuddly, Gru — and we know he'll

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:33.480
be working from a script written by Cinco
Paul and Ken Daurio, who collaborated on the

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:34.870
first two films.

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:36.130
Spider-Man: Homecoming

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:42.640
This new Spidey reboot finds Tom Holland starring
as the web-slinger in a standalone film after

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:48.210
wowing audiences with his debut in Marvel's
Captain America: Civil War.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:54.130
Jon Watts, who helmed the creepy low-budget
Kevin Bacon thriller Cop Car, is on board

00:10:54.130 --> 00:11:00.310
as director for a storyline that features
Robert Downey, Jr.'s Tony Stark playing mentor

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:06.220
to young Spider-Man in his battle against
the Vulture, played by the Birdman himself,

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.710
Michael Keaton.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:09.570
War for the Planet of the Apes

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:14.600
Dawn of the Planet of the Apes director Matt
Reeves returns for this follow-up, which picks

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:21.430
up from Dawn's final scene — a grim foreshadowing
of the major conflict brewing between genetically

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:26.850
enhanced primates and a human population decimated
by the Simian Flu virus.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:32.630
Reeves, who co-wrote the script, is keeping
storyline details under wraps, but says the

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:38.690
events depicted in War for the Planet of the
Apes see Caesar achieving "mythic" status.

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:42.690
That can only mean one thing...catchy songs!

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:53.480
"Yes you finally made a monkey out of meeee!"

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:54.850
Dunkirk

00:11:54.850 --> 00:12:00.500
After a decade spent in the sci-fi/fantasy
realm, writer-director Christopher Nolan has

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:06.830
put his considerable talents to work on a
historical drama about a World War II battle.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:13.430
Dunkirk reunites Nolan with a pair of his
Dark Knight and Inception stars, Tom Hardy

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:19.800
and Cillian Murphy, and early footage hearkens
back to the heart-pounding beachfront battle

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:25.090
imagery in the legendary opening scene from
Saving Private Ryan.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:29.820
Nolan's attention to detail on the partial
IMAX production — including shooting on

00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:35.810
the site of the real-life events that inspired
it — will no doubt serve his tale of heroism

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:38.339
and survival well.

00:12:38.339 --> 00:12:39.899
The Dark Tower

00:12:39.899 --> 00:12:45.950
Of all the adaptations Stephen King's written
works have produced, The Dark Tower has to

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.160
be the most anticipated.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:54.269
The sci-fi western horror film will follow
the events of King's prolific Dark Tower book

00:12:54.269 --> 00:13:00.620
series, presenting the apocalyptic adventure
of an 11-year-old boy named Jake Chambers

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:06.990
as he accidentally uncovers the Mid-World
dimension and joins up with Roland Deschain,

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:08.810
played by Idris Elba.

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:14.940
The two set off to find the Dark Tower before
the Man in Black, played by Matthew McConaughey,

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:19.570
can stop Roland from saving his dimension
from certain destruction.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:24.830
Stephen King's fans are sure to turn up for
this long-overdue Hollywood treatment of the

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.399
beloved series.

00:13:26.399 --> 00:13:27.519
IT

00:13:27.519 --> 00:13:34.800
The 1991 TV miniseries adaptation of Stephen
King's IT amassed a cult following, and Tim

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:41.300
Curry's original performance as the town-terrorizing
clown Pennywise has set a high bar for anyone

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:42.899
to follow in the role.

00:13:42.899 --> 00:13:48.680
So when director Andy Muschietti revealed
his new version of the character, now played

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:54.700
by Bill Skarsgård, in a costume that could've
easily been borrowed from a schoolgirl's dress-up

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:58.430
chest, it's only natural that he faced a little
blowback.

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:01.990
There's still reason to believe this thing
will be a hit, though.

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:07.350
There's tons of talent on board, including
Skarsgård and Finn Wolfhard from Stranger

00:14:07.350 --> 00:14:12.089
Things, and there were plenty of scenes from
the book that were glossed over in the first

00:14:12.089 --> 00:14:13.760
adaptation.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:16.200
Blade Runner 2049

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:23.010
Blade Runner 2049 director Denis Villeneuve
has a few big things going for him — most

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:28.620
importantly, the presence of original Blade
Runner director Ridley Scott, who's producing,

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:33.120
and star Harrison Ford, reprising his role
as Rick Deckard.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:39.490
Ford's joined by an ensemble rounded out by
Ryan Gosling, Robin Wright, and Jared Leto,

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:44.680
all working from a script co-written by Blade
Runner writer Hampton Fancher with Michael

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:45.730
Green.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:50.970
Story details are a mystery, and whether the
end result can stand up alongside the original

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:53.300
obviously remains to be seen.

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:57.680
But all the ingredients are here for a helluva
movie.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:15:00.220
Just keep Deckard away from the fridge.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:11.720
Kingsman: The Golden Circle

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:16.960
The plot details are still a little loose
— rumor has it that the Kingsman British

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:22.079
spy team will team up with their American
equivalents after their headquarters are destroyed

00:15:22.079 --> 00:15:23.829
by a lethal foe.

00:15:23.829 --> 00:15:28.700
But who needs a synopsis when you've got a
cast this intriguingly weird?

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:34.529
Returning stars Taron Egerton, Mark Strong,
and Sophie Cookson are joined by an eclectic

00:15:34.529 --> 00:15:40.950
ensemble that includes Channing Tatum, Halle
Berry, Julianne Moore, Jeff Bridges, and...Elton

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:41.950
John?

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:46.760
"When I was down, I was your clown.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:48.200
Ooh hoo!"

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:53.380
Whatever happens in The Golden Circle, we're
betting it won't be dull.

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:55.839
Friday the 13th Reboot

00:15:55.839 --> 00:16:02.550
Between 1980 and 1989, the hockey-masked slasher
Jason Voorhees hacked his way through scores

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:08.279
of screaming victims in eight films — although
by the end of the decade, the franchise had

00:16:08.279 --> 00:16:12.260
started to teeter between stale and ridiculous.

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:17.940
This latest overhaul arrives nearly a decade
after the last reboot, which grossed nearly

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:18.940
$100 million.

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:24.200
Chances seem good it has to do with a guy
in a hockey mask chopping kids to bits.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:26.440
"Bart do you wanna see my new chainsaw and
hockey mask?!"

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:28.460
"Aaahhh!!!"

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:32.461
"Oh, sorry, what am I thinking?"

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:34.940
Saw: Legacy

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:41.040
Composer Charlie Clouser told The Hollywood
Reporter that the eighth installment of the

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:47.389
Saw franchise will be a "reinvention" of the
series, offering "a fresh take on the material

00:16:47.389 --> 00:16:52.240
that will establish a new storyline and new
characters that can carry the saga into the

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.240
future."

00:16:53.240 --> 00:17:00.230
Expect lots of blood, gore, and puppets involved
in absolutely disgusting and terrifying acts.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:01.230
"Mmmm"

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:02.480
"My tongue out"

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:04.260
"Oh"

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.579
"Hey Dan!"

00:17:06.579 --> 00:17:08.319
Thor: Ragnarok

00:17:08.319 --> 00:17:14.030
In Norse mythology, Ragnarok is basically
the end of the world and the death of the

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.030
gods.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:20.760
So it goes without saying that, based on the
title, Thor: Ragnarok won't be a jolly good

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:23.360
time for our hammer-wielding hero.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:28.459
Although we can guess from his imminent participation
in the upcoming Avengers: Infinity War movies

00:17:28.459 --> 00:17:33.260
that he'll emerge relatively unscathed after
the final act.

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.799
Justice League

00:17:34.799 --> 00:17:40.790
Director Zack Snyder is hard at work on his
third film in the DC Extended Universe, the

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:43.900
superhero team-up film Justice League.

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:49.419
The comic book throwdown ought to reunite
Superman, Batman, and Wonder Woman, while

00:17:49.419 --> 00:17:56.570
also giving formal introductions to Aquaman,
Cyborg, and the movie version of the Flash.

00:17:56.570 --> 00:18:03.750
While we don't yet have any idea what danger
our team will face, we do know it'll be pretty

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:04.750
serious.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:06.910
Star Wars: Episode VIII

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:12.820
This is Star Wars we're talking about, so
the list of things we truly know about Episode

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.280
VIII is awfully short.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:19.860
Pretty much all we can tell you is that this
installment follows the events of Episode

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:25.740
VII, and advances the new trilogy pitting
the Resistance against the First Order led

00:18:25.740 --> 00:18:29.590
by Supreme Leader Snoke and his apprentice
Kylo Ren.

00:18:29.590 --> 00:18:31.650
Oh, and another thing?

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:33.810
It'll probably sell a couple of tickets.

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:35.080
"We're home."

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:41.120
(Audience loses its damn mind)

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.140
Thanks for watching!

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:45.230
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:47.870
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love!

